@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
title The result store — what a run left behind, one file per entry, readable without a process
' purpose: where proveo records a kept sandbox and carried refs after it exits, and what the shell prompt reads
' covers: internal/results/results.go
' covers: internal/results/results_test.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/results.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/results_test.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/teardown.go (recordKept: write-ahead, then settle)
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go (reportCloneRefs: recordCarried)
' covers: internal/run/run.go (ResultsDir, exitStatus, results.SetExit)
' covers: cmd/proveo/prompt.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/prompt_test.go
' covers: e2e/prompt_test.go
' covers: internal/adopt/adopt.go
' covers: internal/adopt/adopt_test.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/verbs.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/verbs_test.go
' covers: internal/sbx/list.go
' covers: internal/sbx/list_test.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/verbs.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/verbs_test.go
' covers: cmd/proveo/clean.go (the reconcile after a clean)
' covers: e2e/teardown_interrupt_test.go
'   why proveo exits instead of staying . _spec/_plans/post-close-surface.puml
'   the decision and its measurements ... _spec/_experiments/terminal-handoff-probes.puml (STARSHIP)
'   the order it lands in ............... _spec/_plans/tui-upgrades-delivery.puml (W6, W7, W8)
'   what teardown decides ............... _spec/internal/backend/teardown.puml
'   what a carried ref is ............... _spec/internal/sbx/clone-workspace.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
' Landed, all 2026-11-10: S1 (the store), S3 (`proveo prompt`), S2 (the write
' points), then S5 (`proveo rm`), S6 (`proveo adopt`), S7 (the reconcile) and
' S8 (the end-of-run lines name the verbs).
'
' ── WHY A STORE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' The Executor, 2026-11-10, on what stays after the agent exits: "proveo
' exits; prompt segment" (D4). proveo does not stay alive to host a surface,
' so whatever a run leaves has to be read later, by a shell prompt, without
' proveo running.
' MEASURED for that decision: `sbx ls` takes 237-483 ms, and a starship
' module is budgeted 500 ms, so the prompt must never call sbx. And "refs to
' adopt" cannot be derived at prompt time: 51 of 57 sessions on this host
' sat only in packed-refs, and 47 of 63 carried refs were already reachable
' from a branch. The count is computed with git while proveo runs, and stored.
'
' ── THE STORE (S1) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' internal/results is a leaf: it imports nothing of proveo's.
'   <state>/results/kept-<sandbox>.json      a sandbox that outlived its run
'   <state>/results/carried-<session>.json   refs home, waiting to be adopted
' ONE FILE PER ENTRY, because three live runs on this host shared one git
' common directory and `proveo clean` removes run directories by pid: a
' single index file would be raced and half-deleted.
' A WRITE IS A RENAME. Put writes a temporary file beside the entry and
' renames it over, so a reader sees the old entry or the new one.
' A KEY IS A FILE NAME, so it is checked: letters, digits, `.`, `_`, `-`.
' List skips a file it cannot parse and a file whose name does not match the
' entry inside it.
' An entry holds: kind, key, repo (symlinks resolved), sid, why, the refs
' with their lead, pending, exit, and when.
'
' ── WHO WRITES (S2) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
'   teardown, at its start    kept-<sandbox>, PENDING: "its teardown did not
'                             finish". A teardown killed outright still
'                             leaves the record that a sandbox exists.
'   teardown, at its end      the entry is settled: removed when the sandbox
'                             was removed (or is a retained OpenCode engine),
'                             else rewritten with why it stays — "the run
'                             failed", the stranded-work message, "its
'                             removal failed", or "teardown stopped by SIGINT
'                             at <step>".
'   the clone carry           carried-<session>: each carried ref that held
'                             commits HEAD lacked, with the count. With none
'                             ahead the entry is removed. reportCloneRefs
'                             writes it, so a sandbox retired at run START
'                             records its refs too.
'   run.Do, on return         the exit status, on every entry of the session.
' The carry now counts the lead of every ref, where it used to stop at the
' first one ahead: one local `git rev-list --count` per ref.
' A store that cannot be written is logged and never fails a run.
'
' ── WHO READS: `proveo prompt` (S3) ────────────────────────────────────────
' A hidden command. It prints one line for the repository the shell is in:
'   1 kept · 2 to adopt
' and nothing when there is nothing, or outside a repository.
'   kept       entries of kind kept whose repo is this one, pending included
'   to adopt   carried refs of this repo with a lead above zero
' IT STARTS NO PROCESS. The repository is the nearest ancestor holding `.git`
' (a directory, or a linked worktree's file), found by reading the
' filesystem. MEASURED: with sbx, git, docker, tmux and starship replaced by
' scripts that log every call, `proveo prompt` logged none.
' MEASURED on a real sandbox, 2026-11-10: a run left by Ctrl+C in teardown
' wrote kept-<sandbox> with exit 130 and why "teardown stopped by SIGINT at
' remove sandbox", and `proveo prompt` in its repository printed "1 kept".
' [Unverified] Nothing reads the store from a shell prompt yet; the starship
' module is the delivery plan's W8.
' e2e runs that do not set PROVEO_STATE_ROOT write into the operator's own
' store. One did, and its entry was removed by hand; the reconcile of the
' next wave drops entries whose repository is gone.
'
' ── THE VERBS THAT LOWER THE COUNTS (S5, S6) ──────────────────────────────
' A count nobody can lower is a nag. Each number in the prompt has a command.
' `proveo rm [sandbox]` — the kept count.
'   with no argument it lists the kept sandboxes, this repository's first
'   it REFUSES A RUNNING SANDBOX unless --stop asks it to run `sbx stop`
'     first (R2, the operator: "Do not stop sandboxes implicitly"); the
'     refusal names `proveo rm --stop <name>`
'   it LIFTS THE OUTPUT DIR the launch receipt records (OutputDir), so a
'     sandbox a failed lift kept gives its output up (R2, F6)
'   it CARRIES BEFORE IT REMOVES. The Input the carry needs is rebuilt from
'     `sbx ls --json` (the workspace, the agent) and the store's entry (the
'     repository). Work that cannot come home keeps the sandbox, and the
'     error names `sbx rm --force` as the way to delete it regardless
'   then `sbx rm --force`, the launch receipt, and the entry
'   a sandbox sbx no longer lists is already gone: only the entry is cleared
' AN EMPTY LISTING CLEARS NOTHING. sbx prints an empty listing when its daemon
' is busy as well as when the host is empty, so `rm` and the reconcile refuse
' to conclude anything from one: "sbx gave no listing … nothing was changed".
' `proveo adopt [ref|session]` — the to-adopt count.
'   with no argument it lists every ref under refs/proveo/ that holds
'     commits no local branch holds — read from git, so refs that predate
'     the store are listed too
'   it takes a ref, a session, or a branch name one session carried; a name
'     that fits several refs is an error that lists them
'   IT CREATES THE BRANCH AND NOTHING ELSE (the Executor, D11: "Create the
'     branch only"). `git branch <name> <ref>`: HEAD, the index and the files
'     stay, which keeps clone mode's promise that a run does not touch the
'     checkout. An existing branch of that name is refused, with `--as`.
' WHAT "TO ADOPT" COUNTS changed with the verbs. A ref's lead is the number
' of its commits that NO LOCAL BRANCH holds (`git rev-list --count <ref>
' --not --branches`), where S2 first counted against HEAD. So creating a
' branch, by `proveo adopt` or by hand, lowers the count with no bookkeeping,
' and so does merging the work.
' TWO REFS AT ONE COMMIT COUNT ONCE. `proveo rm` carries again, under its own
' session name, so the same commit can sit under two refs. MEASURED on a real
' sandbox: the prompt read "2 to adopt" for one commit. Each ref now records
' its tip, and the summary counts distinct tips.
'
' ── STALE ENTRIES ARE DROPPED WHERE GIT AND sbx ARE AT HAND (S7) ───────────
' ReconcileResults runs at run start, in `rm`, in `adopt` and after `clean`:
'   a kept entry whose sandbox a non-empty listing no longer holds
'   a carried entry whose repository directory is gone
'   for the repository at hand, a carried ref that was deleted or that a
'     branch now holds; the entry goes when none is left
' Another repository's carried entries are left alone: nothing is at hand to
' judge them with. The prompt never reconciles; it only reads.
' MEASURED 2026-11-10: a clone e2e had left a carried entry for a temporary
' repository in the operator's own store; `proveo rm` with no argument
' removed it.
'
' ── THE END-OF-RUN LINES NAME THE VERBS (S8; reshaped by R2, 2026-11-11) ──
'   ⚠ <name> — kept for diagnosis | kept: <why>
'       `proveo rm --stop <name>` carries its work home and removes it
' The dim fix names --stop while the sandbox runs (every measured kept
' sandbox was running), plain `proveo rm <name>` once it is stopped, and it
' goes to the run log when the operator's Ctrl+C caused the keep (decision
' E). The review and adopt commands, and `sbx exec -it <name> bash`, are
' run-log rows now: the branches fact names each ref with new commits, the
' prompt segment counts them and `proveo adopt` lists them. The rescue line
' after a removal that timed out still names sbx's own commands; proveo
' cannot do better than sbx there.
' WHY THE STORE RECORDS: "the run failed", "teardown stopped by SIGINT at
' remove sandbox", "its removal failed", and a stranded carry's own words,
' which now say "it" ("the agent's branches are still only in it").
'
' Pinned by internal/backend/sandbox/verbs_test.go:
'   TestRemoveKeptClearsNothingOnAListingItCannotTrust
'   TestRemoveKeptRefusesARunningSandboxAndForgetsAGoneOne
'   TestRemoveKeptCarriesThenRemovesAStoppedSandbox
'   TestRemoveKeptKeepsASandboxWhoseWorkCannotComeHome
'   TestRemoveKeptStopsARunningSandboxOnlyWhenAsked
'   TestKeptInputLiftsTheOutputDirTheReceiptRecords
'   TestReconcileDropsOnlyWhatIsProvablyGone
' by internal/adopt/adopt_test.go:
'   TestCarriedListsEachRefWithTheWorkNoBranchHolds
'   TestPickTakesARefASessionOrAnUnambiguousBranch
'   TestBranchCreatesTheBranchAndMovesNothingElse
' by cmd/proveo/verbs_test.go:
'   TestAdoptCreatesTheBranchLeavesTheCheckoutAloneAndLowersThePromptCount
'   TestAdoptOutsideARepositoryRefuses
'   TestRmWithoutAnArgumentListsWhatWasKept
' by internal/sbx/list_test.go: TestListReadsBothShapesAndSaysWhenThereIsNoListing
' and on a real sandbox by e2e TestCtrlCInTeardownSaysOnceThenLeavesWith130:
'   `proveo rm` refused it while it ran, naming --stop, then carried it,
'   removed it and cleared its entry.
'
' Pinned by internal/results/results_test.go:
'   TestAnEntryRoundTripsAndReplacesItsPredecessor
'   TestAKeyThatCouldLeaveTheStoreIsRefused
'   TestListSkipsWhatItCannotTrust
'   TestTheSummaryCountsThisRepositorysEntries
'   TestRepoOfFindsTheCheckoutFromInsideIt
'   TestSetExitMarksOnlyTheSessionsEntries
' by internal/backend/sandbox/results_test.go:
'   TestTeardownWritesAheadThenSettlesTheKeptEntry
'   TestAStoppedTeardownRecordsTheSandboxItLeft
'   TestAStrandedCarryKeepsAnEntryNamingTheWork
'   TestTheCarryRecordsEachRefThatHoldsWorkHEADLacks
' by cmd/proveo/prompt_test.go:
'   TestTheLeftLineCountsWhatThisRepositoryWasLeft
'   TestThePromptCommandIsHiddenAndPrintsOneLine
' and by e2e: TestThePromptCommandStartsNoProcess,
'   TestCtrlCInTeardownSaysOnceThenLeavesWith130 (real sbx)

component "teardown\nwrites ahead, then settles" as TD <<app>>
component "the clone carry\nrefs and their lead" as CARRY <<app>>
component """run.Do""\nthe exit status" as DO <<app>>
database """<state>/results/""\none JSON file per entry" as STORE <<db>>
component """proveo prompt""\nhidden · starts no process" as PROMPT <<host>>
component "the shell prompt\n""1 kept · 2 to adopt""" as SHELL <<host>>
component """proveo rm"" · ""proveo adopt""\nthe verbs that lower the counts" as VERBS <<app>>
component """sbx ls"" at prompt time\n**237-483 ms, over the budget**" as SLOW <<error>>

TD ARROW_MAIN STORE : kept-<sandbox>
CARRY ARROW_MAIN STORE : carried-<session>
DO ARROW_OPTIONAL STORE : exit
STORE ARROW_MAIN PROMPT : read only
PROMPT ARROW_MAIN SHELL
SLOW ARROW_ERROR SHELL : what the store avoids
SHELL ARROW_OPTIONAL VERBS : the operator acts
VERBS ARROW_MAIN STORE : clear, after carrying or branching

note bottom of STORE
  **One file per entry, written by rename.**
  Live runs share a state directory, and a
  single index would be raced. A reader sees
  an old entry or a new one, never half.
end note

note bottom of TD
  **Written before it is true.** The entry is
  put down pending when teardown starts, so a
  teardown that is killed still leaves a
  record that the sandbox exists.
end note

note bottom of PROMPT
  **No process, every time.** A shell runs it
  before each prompt. It finds the repository
  by walking up to "".git"" and counts files; it
  never calls git or sbx.
end note

note bottom of VERBS
  **Carry first; branch only.** ""rm"" brings a
  kept sandbox's work home before removing
  it and refuses a running one. ""adopt"" makes
  a branch and leaves HEAD and files alone.
end note

note bottom of CARRY
  **Counted while git is at hand.** Most
  carried refs are already on a branch. Only
  a ref HEAD lacked commits from counts, and
  the count is stored, not derived later.
end note
@enduml
